=== p2-windows · W7 · page:admin/TeslaFeatureFlags (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:admin/TeslaFeatureFlags   kind=page   web route=/tesla-features
Web source  : web/src/features/admin/pages/TeslaFeatureFlagsPage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) + Windows App SDK workload — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.ViewModel.cs (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs
  (the Fluent view), exactly as the sibling W7 ApiLogsPage / FeedbackQueuePage do. The generated prompt's idealized
  "TeslaFeatureFlagsPage.xaml + TeslaFeatureFlagsPageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Admin" is mapped onto
  these real conventions; the surface registers itself with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name
  ("TeslaFeatureFlags", already in RouteTable.cs → /tesla-features, RouteGroup.AdminDevTools).
- Web parity shape: TeslaFeatureFlagsPage.tsx is a thin <PageContainer title subtitle> wrapper around the shared
  <FeatureToggles /> component (features/settings/components/FeatureToggles.tsx). The native port is the same
  one-to-one composition: the W2 TsPageContainer (the native port of the web PageContainer) bound to the page
  title/subtitle, hosting the existing W3 FeatureToggles control (feature-views/FeatureToggles.cs) as its body via
  PageContent. The page is pure chrome — the hosted surface already owns the feature-config read
  (useTeslaFeatureConfig), the refresh mutation (useRefreshTeslaFeatureConfig) and the loading/empty/error data
  states — so it is NOT re-implemented (DRY). This matches the manifest record: page has no API data sources and no
  named panels of its own; its parity scope is the two header strings.
- Data binding (ADR-004): the page has no query of its own. The W4 shell factory constructs the page parameterless,
  so it defaults to a new EmptyFeatureTogglesSource (the same host-injection precedent ApiLogsPage/FeedbackQueuePage
  use via their Empty*Feed defaults): it yields a single Loaded snapshot with zero entries so the hosted
  FeatureToggles lands on its friendly empty state rather than a perpetual spinner, and its refresh is a no-op
  success. A host that owns the repository passes the repository-backed FeatureTogglesSource instead — no view
  change. The page state holder (TeslaFeatureFlagsPageViewModel) exposes the localized Title/Subtitle the header
  binds to and records the PII-safe view.opened diagnostic once on LoadAsync.
- SI units N/A (no unit-bearing fields on this surface).
- i18n: the two parity keys (translation.featureConfig.title / translation.featureConfig.subtitle) already exist
  verbatim in Strings/{en,he,ar}/Resources.resw (the FeatureToggles component owns them); the page reuses the SAME
  keys through FeatureTogglesRegistration.TitleKey/SubtitleKey so the page header and the hosted panel header can
  never drift. No new catalog rows required; zero hardcoded literals.
- a11y / dark mode: AutomationProperties.SetName on the page root; TsPageContainer's TsPageHeader emits the H1
  heading level; the hosted FeatureToggles carries its own Narrator names + LiveRegion announcements. All color and
  typography come from design tokens (TsPageContainer / FeatureToggles) — no hardcoded brushes.
- Pre-existing blocker repaired: TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj had been re-corrupted by its documented .gitattributes
  merge=union strategy into TWO <Project> roots (lines 1-1379 + 1380-2778) with a stranded third </Project>, mixed
  CRLF/LF endings, and 2633 Compile items / 1327 distinct — failing XML load (MSB4025/MSB4067) and blocking the
  whole-solution build + test at baseline. Regenerated per the file's own INVARIANT into the single canonical
  Project root: the case-insensitive ordinal path-sorted, Include-deduplicated UNION of all 1327 Microsoft.UI-free
  sources (each verified present on disk; Missing=0) plus the two new TeslaFeatureFlagsPage Model/ViewModel links
  (1329 total), all LF + final newline. The .cs view stays out of the headless project (it uses Microsoft.UI).

=== PARITY ===
PARITY_REQUIRED=2

# Strings (2) — every visible literal resolves from Strings/*.resw via the ILocalizer facade with the web key names.
#   The page header binds Title/Subtitle from the bound state holder (TeslaFeatureFlagsPageViewModel) and the
#   TsPageContainer (web PageContainer) renders them; both keys are owned once by FeatureTogglesRegistration so the
#   page header and the hosted FeatureToggles panel header resolve identical copy.
[x] string - featureConfig.title    -> TeslaFeatureFlagsRegistration.Title (TeslaFeatureFlagsPage.Model.cs) ->
             FeatureTogglesRegistration.Title localizer.GetString("translation.featureConfig.title", "Feature Flags");
             bound via TeslaFeatureFlagsPageViewModel.Title (TeslaFeatureFlagsPage.ViewModel.cs) -> TsPageContainer.Title
             (TeslaFeatureFlagsPage.cs). Tests: Registration_resolves_the_two_parity_string_keys_through_the_facade,
             ViewModel_title_and_subtitle_resolve_through_the_facade, ViewModel_exposes_localized_title_and_subtitle.
[x] string - featureConfig.subtitle -> TeslaFeatureFlagsRegistration.Subtitle (TeslaFeatureFlagsPage.Model.cs) ->
             FeatureTogglesRegistration.Subtitle localizer.GetString("translation.featureConfig.subtitle",
             "Tesla account feature configuration"); bound via TeslaFeatureFlagsPageViewModel.Subtitle ->
             TsPageContainer.Subtitle (TeslaFeatureFlagsPage.cs). Tests as above.

